<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3218" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">appulsus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adp-</span></b> ), ūs, m.
		1. appello, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a driving to</i> some place. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In the lit. signif. only in the
			jurists: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecoris,</span>”
				<i>a driving of a flock to drink</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					43, 19, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A landing</i>, <i>bringing to
			land</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab litorum appulsu arcere, Liv, 27, 30: oppidum
					celerrimum adpulsu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					3, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">utrinque prora paratam semper adpulsui frontem
					agit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. G.
				44</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>An approaching</i>, <i>approach</i>,
			in gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pars terrae adpulsu solis exarsit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 1, 10, 24</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>An effect</i>, <i>influence caused by
				approach</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frigoris et caloris adpulsus sentire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 56, 141</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deorum adpulsu homines somniare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Div. 1, 30 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
